Newspeak3
'PlatformFactory'
(* The module behind the platform a module is handed (§8.3): a shipped
   core-library module, booted by the host with the VM mirror and the
   kernel instance (`docs/design/core-library.md`, "The module table and
   the boot").

   The factory pattern: this root holds what is privileged -- the mirror
   and the kernel -- and the host never hands its instance to anyone. It
   instantiates the root once, sends it `newPlatform`, its one public
   member, and hands every program that platform, an instance of the
   nested class `Platform`, whose factory is a harmless `new`. What a
   program may instantiate are the nested classes, the facets, which it
   reaches only through the platform's class accessors and members; each
   reaches the mirror and the kernel lexically, as a member of this root,
   never through a slot of its own, so a program can make as many
   platforms, transcripts and namespaces as it likes and every one of them
   writes through the one mirror. The nested classes are private, so even
   a holder of this root's instance could send it nothing but
   `newPlatform`: a second line of defence behind the instance being
   unreachable. Nothing a program can name answers this root's instance or its
   class, so no program can build a second one over something that is not
   the mirror. Keep it so: no code whose receiver is this root's instance
   may send it anything it does not understand, since a
   `MessageNotUnderstood` hands its receiver to whoever catches it
   (`docs/design/core-library.md`, "No program reaches a shipped module's
   root").

   The factory's parameters are copied into slots because neither a lazy
   slot nor a method may name them (§6). A send to `vmMirror` here is a
   mirror send, as in `Kernel.ns`: this module is resolved with
   `resolve_kernel`, which only shipped source is.

   Everything here is a value (§3.1.1), as SOMns's `Platform` is: stateless
   but for what the host hands the root. *)
class PlatformFactory usingVmMirror: theMirror kernel: theKernel = Object <: Value (
    | private vmMirror = theMirror.
      private kernelModule = theKernel. |
) (
    (* §8.3 describes the platform as an object that "provides accessors to
       various modules"; each is a lazy slot (§6.3.3), built on first use,
       so a program pays only for what it asks for. The module's classes
       are handed out by class accessors, each exactly `^outer
       PlatformFactory <Name>`, which an image names by its path from the
       platform rather than carrying the class
       (`docs/design/image-format.md`, "The platform path section"). Each
       is a lexical send, which reaches the root's private classes (§5.9). *)
    private class Platform = Value new () (
        lazy public transcript = Transcript new.
        lazy public collections = Collections new.
        lazy public kernel = KernelNamespace new.
        public Platform = ( ^outer PlatformFactory Platform )
        public Transcript = ( ^outer PlatformFactory Transcript )
        public Collections = ( ^outer PlatformFactory Collections )
        public KernelNamespace = ( ^outer PlatformFactory KernelNamespace )
    )
    private class Transcript = Value new () (
        public show: text = ( ^vmMirror transcript: self show: text ifFail: [^super show: text] )
        public newLine = ( ^vmMirror transcriptNewLine: self ifFail: [^super newLine] )
    )
    (* The Core Library's `collections` namespace, whose one member is the
       one a whitelisted corpus module asks for (`docs/design/core-library.md`,
       "The on-demand rule"). *)
    private class Collections = Value new () (
        public List = ( ^OrderedCollection )
    )
    (* `platform kernel`: the kernel classes a program may name, as
       Primordial Soup's `Kernel wrapping:` facet answers them. *)
    private class KernelNamespace = Value new () (
        public Exception = ( ^kernelModule Exception )
        public Error = ( ^kernelModule Error )
        public MessageNotUnderstood = ( ^kernelModule MessageNotUnderstood )
        public Halt = ( ^kernelModule Halt )
        public Message = ( ^kernelModule Message )
    )
    (* The one public member: the platform the host hands out. *)
    public newPlatform = ( ^Platform new )
) : ()
